## Choose the right interface

OData exposes application data through a service. ADT exposes development repository capabilities. A reachable OData service does not imply source-code read, object creation, or activation access.

## Keep reads bounded

- Name the service and entity set explicitly.
- Request only needed fields and a small, intentional number of rows.
- Avoid persisting sample business values in workflow history or logs unless an approved business need requires it.
- Surface timeouts, authentication failures, and SAP errors without exposing credentials.
- Re-check the service's authorization and data-handling rules with the SAP owner.

## Transport note

HTTP does not encrypt credentials or returned business data in transit. Use only on a network path whose transport protection and access controls are accepted for the environment; prefer properly trusted HTTPS where available.
